# TableViewModel

`TableViewModel` describes the structure of the table. Everything you render reads from `vm.current`: plain reactive values backed by `$derived`, so a template that reads them updates when the data or any plugin state changes.

```ts
const vm = table.createViewModel(columns)
// vm.current.headerRows, vm.current.pageRows, vm.current.tableAttrs, ...
// vm.flatColumns, vm.pluginStates, vm._debug
```

<Admonition type="info">v7 removed the store fields (<code>vm.rows</code>, <code>vm.headerRows</code>, ...). <code>Subscribe</code> was removed in v7; see <a href="/docs/guides/migrating-to-v7">Migrating to v7</a>.</Admonition>

## Usage

### `TableViewModel#current: ViewModelCurrent`

The reactive values of the table: `tableAttrs`, `tableHeadAttrs`, `tableBodyAttrs`, `visibleColumns`, `headerRows`, `originalRows`, `rows` and `pageRows`. Combined with `row.current` and `cell.current`, that is the whole rendering surface:

```svelte
<table {...vm.current.tableAttrs}>
    <thead {...vm.current.tableHeadAttrs}>
        {#each vm.current.headerRows as headerRow (headerRow.id)}
            <tr {...headerRow.current.attrs}>
                {#each headerRow.cells as cell (cell.id)}
                    <th {...cell.current.attrs}><Render of={cell.render()} /></th>
                {/each}
            </tr>
        {/each}
    </thead>
    <tbody {...vm.current.tableBodyAttrs}>
        {#each vm.current.pageRows as row (row.id)}
            <tr {...row.current.attrs}>
                {#each row.cells as cell (cell.id)}
                    <td {...cell.current.attrs}><Render of={cell.render()} /></td>
                {/each}
            </tr>
        {/each}
    </tbody>
</table>
```

A read inside a template, `$derived` or `$effect` is tracked. A read anywhere else (a `load` function, a test, server rendering) returns the current value.

### Attributes

#### `TableViewModel#current.tableAttrs: TableAttributes`

Attributes to spread onto the `<table>` element.

#### `TableViewModel#current.tableHeadAttrs: TableHeadAttributes`

Attributes to spread onto the `<thead>` element.

#### `TableViewModel#current.tableBodyAttrs: TableBodyAttributes`

Attributes to spread onto the `<tbody>` element.

### Rows

#### `TableViewModel#current.headerRows: HeaderRow[]`

The <a href="/docs/api/header-row">`HeaderRow`</a>s that represent `<tr>` elements in `<thead>`.

```svelte
<thead>
    {#each vm.current.headerRows as headerRow (headerRow.id)}
        <tr {...headerRow.current.attrs}>...</tr>
    {/each}
</thead>
```

#### `TableViewModel#current.rows: BodyRow[]`

The <a href="/docs/api/body-row">`BodyRow`</a>s that represent `<tr>` elements in `<tbody>`, after every plugin's row transformation.

```svelte
<tbody>
    {#each vm.current.rows as row (row.id)}
        <tr {...row.current.attrs}>...</tr>
    {/each}
</tbody>
```

#### `TableViewModel#current.pageRows: BodyRow[]`

The `BodyRow`s **of the current page**.

`current.pageRows` is affected by pagination plugins while `current.rows` is not. Without a pagination plugin the two are equal.

```svelte
<tbody>
    {#each vm.current.pageRows as row (row.id)}
        <tr {...row.current.attrs}>...</tr>
    {/each}
</tbody>
```

#### `TableViewModel#current.originalRows: BodyRow[]`

The `BodyRow`s built from the data, before any plugin transformation.

### Columns

#### `TableViewModel#current.visibleColumns: FlatColumn[]`

The flat columns left after every plugin's column transformation (hidden columns removed, order applied). Useful for a `colspan` that spans the whole table:

```svelte
<th colspan={vm.current.visibleColumns.length}>...</th>
```

#### `TableViewModel#flatColumns: FlatColumn[]`

The flat columns of the table before plugin transformations. This is a plain array, not reactive: the column definitions do not change after the view model is built.

Flat columns usually represent the last row of columns in your header, which includes data columns and display columns. They are distinct from group columns which must by definition be one row above other columns.

### Plugins

#### `TableViewModel#pluginStates: PluginStates`

The state each plugin exposes, keyed by the name you gave the plugin in `createTable`. Plugin state is made of `Box`, `ReadonlyBox`, `RecordSet` and `ArraySet` values: read and write their `current` property.

```ts
const { pageIndex, hasNextPage } = vm.pluginStates.page
if (hasNextPage.current) pageIndex.current += 1
```

<Admonition type="tip">See also <a href="/docs/plugins/overview#controlling-plugin-state">Plugin State</a>.</Admonition>

### Debugging

#### `TableViewModel#_debug: ViewModelDebug`

Counters for performance work: `pluginCount`, `pluginNames`, `derivedCount` (derivations per chain, e.g. `derivedCount.rows`), `derivationCalls` and `derivationTimings` per derivation, plus `resetCounters()`, `getTotalCalls()` and `getTotalMs()`. The shape may change between minor versions; do not build features on it.
